{"id":"n5_u02_l1","unit_id":"n5_u02","instructional_level":"N5","title":"The h and m rows","goal":"Add ten kana and read your first shop and nature words, on the way to your first stamp in Tokyo.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_h_ha","ka_h_hi","ka_h_fu","ka_h_he","ka_h_ho","ka_h_ma","ka_h_mi","ka_h_mu","ka_h_me","ka_h_mo"],"vocab":["v_hito","v_fune","v_hoshi","v_machi","v_mise","v_mochi","v_mushi","v_kumo","v_hana","v_okane"]},"explain":[{"heading":"The h row and the m row","body":["は ひ ふ へ ほ read ha, hi, fu, he, ho. ふ is a soft sound made with both lips, between \"h\" and \"f\". ま み む め も read ma, mi, mu, me, mo.","Look-alikes to watch: は and ほ, め and ぬ (from last unit), ま and も."],"examples":[{"ja":"ひと","reading":"hito","en":"person"},{"ja":"まち","reading":"machi","en":"town"},{"ja":"くも","reading":"kumo","en":"cloud"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_kr01","q_n5u02_kr02","q_n5u02_kr03","q_n5u02_mt01","q_n5u02_mt02","q_n5u02_rc01","q_n5u02_rc02","q_n5u02_vm_hito","q_n5u02_vm_fune","q_n5u02_vm_hoshi","q_n5u02_vm_machi","q_n5u02_vm_mise","q_n5u02_vm_mochi","q_n5u02_vm_mushi","q_n5u02_vm_kumo","q_n5u02_vm_hana","q_n5u02_vm_okane"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ha","ka_h_hi","ka_h_fu","ka_h_he","ka_h_ho","ka_h_ma","ka_h_mi","ka_h_mu","ka_h_me","ka_h_mo"],"n":6},{"type":"kana_listen","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ha","ka_h_hi","ka_h_fu","ka_h_he","ka_h_ho","ka_h_ma","ka_h_mi","ka_h_mu","ka_h_me","ka_h_mo"],"n":4}]},"exit_check":{"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ha","ka_h_hi","ka_h_fu","ka_h_he","ka_h_ho","ka_h_ma","ka_h_mi","ka_h_mu","ka_h_me","ka_h_mo"],"n":6},{"type":"vocab_meaning","from":"vocab","ids":["v_hito","v_fune","v_hoshi","v_machi","v_mise","v_mochi","v_mushi","v_kumo","v_hana","v_okane"],"n":4}],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u02_l2","unit_id":"n5_u02","instructional_level":"N5","title":"The y, r and w rows, and ん","goal":"Finish the basic hiragana chart. After this lesson you can read every basic kana.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_h_ya","ka_h_yu","ka_h_yo","ka_h_ra","ka_h_ri","ka_h_ru","ka_h_re","ka_h_ro","ka_h_wa","ka_h_wo","ka_h_n"],"vocab":["v_yama","v_yuki","v_yoru","v_sakura","v_onna","v_hon","v_sensei","v_nihon","v_watashi","v_kawa","v_sora","v_haru","v_roku","v_kuruma","v_yasai","v_yume","v_kotori","v_atarashii","v_furui","v_youkoso"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Three groups","body":["The y row has only three kana: や ゆ よ (ya, yu, yo). The r row, ら り る れ ろ, uses a sound between English \"r\" and \"l\": a quick tap of the tongue behind your top teeth.","わ is \"wa\". を is pronounced \"o\" and is used only as a grammar word (you will meet it in a later unit). ん is a single consonant \"n\" that takes a full beat of its own."],"examples":[{"ja":"さくら","reading":"sakura","en":"cherry blossom"},{"ja":"ほん","reading":"hon","en":"book (2 beats: ho-n)"},{"ja":"わたし","reading":"watashi","en":"I"}]},{"heading":"Welcome to Japan","body":["ようこそ means \"welcome\". You will see it on signs in Tokyo."],"examples":[{"ja":"ようこそ","reading":"youkoso","en":"welcome"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_kr04","q_n5u02_kr05","q_n5u02_kr06","q_n5u02_kr07","q_n5u02_mt03","q_n5u02_rc03","q_n5u02_rc04","q_n5u02_vm_yama","q_n5u02_vm_yuki","q_n5u02_vm_yoru","q_n5u02_vm_sakura","q_n5u02_vm_onna","q_n5u02_vm_hon","q_n5u02_vm_sensei","q_n5u02_vm_nihon"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ya","ka_h_yu","ka_h_yo","ka_h_ra","ka_h_ri","ka_h_ru","ka_h_re","ka_h_ro","ka_h_wa","ka_h_wo","ka_h_n"],"n":6},{"type":"kana_recall","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ya","ka_h_yu","ka_h_yo","ka_h_ra","ka_h_ri","ka_h_ru","ka_h_re","ka_h_ro","ka_h_wa","ka_h_wo","ka_h_n"],"n":4}]},"exit_check":{"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ma","ka_h_mi","ka_h_mu","ka_h_me","ka_h_mo","ka_h_ya","ka_h_yu","ka_h_yo","ka_h_ra","ka_h_ri","ka_h_ru","ka_h_re","ka_h_ro","ka_h_wa","ka_h_wo","ka_h_n"],"n":6},{"type":"vocab_meaning","from":"vocab","ids":["v_yama","v_yuki","v_yoru","v_sakura","v_onna","v_hon","v_sensei","v_nihon","v_watashi","v_kawa","v_sora","v_haru","v_roku","v_kuruma","v_yasai","v_yume","v_kotori","v_atarashii","v_furui","v_youkoso"],"n":4}],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u02_l3","unit_id":"n5_u02","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Voiced sounds: g, z and d","goal":"Learn the two small dots (dakuten) that voice a consonant: k to g, s to z, t to d.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_h_ga","ka_h_gi","ka_h_gu","ka_h_ge","ka_h_go","ka_h_za","ka_h_ji","ka_h_zu","ka_h_ze","ka_h_zo","ka_h_da","ka_h_dji","ka_h_dzu","ka_h_de","ka_h_do"],"vocab":["v_gohan","v_nihongo","v_eiga","v_kagi","v_tomodachi","v_denwa","v_douzo","v_zou","v_mado","v_mizu","v_deguchi","v_iriguchi","v_ringo","v_kodomo"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Two small dots","body":["Add two small dots (゛, called dakuten) to a kana and its consonant becomes voiced: か ka becomes が ga, さ sa becomes ざ za, た ta becomes だ da.","Special cases: じ is \"ji\" (from し), ず is \"zu\" (from す), で is \"de\", and ぢ and づ sound the same as じ and ず. ぢ and づ are rare; you mostly see じ and ず."],"examples":[{"ja":"ごはん","reading":"gohan","en":"rice, a meal"},{"ja":"ともだち","reading":"tomodachi","en":"friend"},{"ja":"でぐち","reading":"deguchi","en":"exit"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_kr08","q_n5u02_kr09","q_n5u02_kr11","q_n5u02_mt04","q_n5u02_mt05","q_n5u02_rc05","q_n5u02_rc06","q_n5u02_vm_gohan","q_n5u02_vm_nihongo","q_n5u02_vm_eiga","q_n5u02_vm_kagi","q_n5u02_vm_tomodachi","q_n5u02_vm_denwa","q_n5u02_vm_douzo","q_n5u02_vm_zou"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ga","ka_h_gi","ka_h_gu","ka_h_ge","ka_h_go","ka_h_za","ka_h_ji","ka_h_zu","ka_h_ze","ka_h_zo","ka_h_da","ka_h_dji","ka_h_dzu","ka_h_de","ka_h_do"],"n":6},{"type":"kana_listen","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ga","ka_h_gi","ka_h_gu","ka_h_ge","ka_h_go","ka_h_za","ka_h_ji","ka_h_zu","ka_h_ze","ka_h_zo","ka_h_da","ka_h_dji","ka_h_dzu","ka_h_de","ka_h_do"],"n":4}]},"exit_check":{"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ga","ka_h_gi","ka_h_gu","ka_h_ge","ka_h_go","ka_h_za","ka_h_ji","ka_h_zu","ka_h_ze","ka_h_zo","ka_h_da","ka_h_dji","ka_h_dzu","ka_h_de","ka_h_do"],"n":6},{"type":"vocab_meaning","from":"vocab","ids":["v_gohan","v_nihongo","v_eiga","v_kagi","v_tomodachi","v_denwa","v_douzo","v_zou","v_mado","v_mizu","v_deguchi","v_iriguchi","v_ringo","v_kodomo"],"n":4}],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u02_l4","unit_id":"n5_u02","instructional_level":"N5","title":"B and P sounds","goal":"Finish the chart: two dots make b, and a small circle makes p.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_h_ba","ka_h_bi","ka_h_bu","ka_h_be","ka_h_bo","ka_h_pa","ka_h_pi","ka_h_pu","ka_h_pe","ka_h_po"],"vocab":["v_kaban","v_tabemono","v_enpitsu","v_boushi","v_tenpura","v_pan","v_sanpo","v_budou","v_obentou","v_shinbun"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Dots and a circle","body":["は ha with two dots is ば ba; with a small circle (゜, called handakuten) it is ぱ pa. The same works for ひ, ふ, へ, ほ.","You have now met all the basic hiragana. Next comes combining them (small ゃ ゅ ょ and っ) in the next unit."],"examples":[{"ja":"かばん","reading":"kaban","en":"bag"},{"ja":"ぱん","reading":"pan","en":"bread"},{"ja":"しんぶん","reading":"shinbun","en":"newspaper"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_kr10","q_n5u02_kr12","q_n5u02_mt06","q_n5u02_mt07","q_n5u02_rc07","q_n5u02_rc08","q_n5u02_vm_kaban","q_n5u02_vm_tabemono","q_n5u02_vm_enpitsu","q_n5u02_vm_boushi","q_n5u02_vm_tenpura","q_n5u02_vm_pan"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ba","ka_h_bi","ka_h_bu","ka_h_be","ka_h_bo","ka_h_pa","ka_h_pi","ka_h_pu","ka_h_pe","ka_h_po"],"n":6},{"type":"kana_recall","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ba","ka_h_bi","ka_h_bu","ka_h_be","ka_h_bo","ka_h_pa","ka_h_pi","ka_h_pu","ka_h_pe","ka_h_po"],"n":4}]},"exit_check":{"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_ga","ka_h_gi","ka_h_gu","ka_h_ge","ka_h_go","ka_h_za","ka_h_ji","ka_h_zu","ka_h_ze","ka_h_zo","ka_h_da","ka_h_dji","ka_h_dzu","ka_h_de","ka_h_do","ka_h_ba","ka_h_bi","ka_h_bu","ka_h_be","ka_h_bo","ka_h_pa","ka_h_pi","ka_h_pu","ka_h_pe","ka_h_po"],"n":6},{"type":"vocab_meaning","from":"vocab","ids":["v_kaban","v_tabemono","v_enpitsu","v_boushi","v_tenpura","v_pan","v_sanpo","v_budou","v_obentou","v_shinbun"],"n":4}],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u02_l5","unit_id":"n5_u02","instructional_level":"N5","title":"First greetings","goal":"Say hello, thank you and goodbye politely: the words you will use the moment you arrive in Tokyo.","introduces":{"vocab":["v_ohayou","v_ohayougozaimasu","v_konnichiwa","v_konbanwa","v_oyasuminasai","v_arigatou","v_arigatougozaimasu","v_douitashimashite","v_sumimasen","v_gomennasai","v_sayounara","v_hajimemashite","v_yoroshiku","v_hai","v_iie","v_itadakimasu","v_gochisousama","v_tadaima","v_okaerinasai"],"grammar":["g_greeting_set"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Casual and polite","body":["Greetings are fixed phrases. To be polite to strangers, shopkeepers and older people, use the longer form: おはようございます, ありがとうございます.","With friends and family the short form is fine: おはよう, ありがとう."],"examples":[{"ja":"おはようございます","reading":"ohayou gozaimasu","en":"Good morning (polite)"},{"ja":"ありがとうございます","reading":"arigatou gozaimasu","en":"Thank you (polite)"}]},{"heading":"Across the day","body":["こんにちは (hello, good afternoon) and こんばんは (good evening) end in は, which is pronounced \"wa\" here. おやすみなさい is only for going to bed. すみません is the all-purpose \"excuse me / sorry / thanks for the trouble\"."],"examples":[{"ja":"こんにちは","reading":"konnichiwa","en":"Hello / good afternoon"},{"ja":"すみません","reading":"sumimasen","en":"Excuse me"}]},{"heading":"Meeting and meals","body":["はじめまして is said when you meet someone for the first time; after your name you add よろしくおねがいします. At meals say いただきます before eating and ごちそうさまでした afterwards. At home, ただいま is answered with おかえりなさい."],"examples":[{"ja":"はじめまして","reading":"hajimemashite","en":"Nice to meet you"},{"ja":"ただいま","reading":"tadaima","en":"I'm home"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_gm01","q_n5u02_gm02","q_n5u02_gm03","q_n5u02_gm04","q_n5u02_gm05","q_n5u02_gm06","q_n5u02_dg01","q_n5u02_dg02","q_n5u02_vm_ohayou","q_n5u02_vm_ohayougozaimasu","q_n5u02_vm_konnichiwa","q_n5u02_vm_konbanwa","q_n5u02_vm_oyasuminasai","q_n5u02_vm_arigatou","q_n5u02_vm_arigatougozaimasu","q_n5u02_vm_douitashimashite"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_dg03","q_n5u02_dg04","q_n5u02_dg05","q_n5u02_dg06","q_n5u02_dg07","q_n5u02_dg08","q_n5u02_ty05","q_n5u02_ty06","q_n5u02_ty07","q_n5u02_ty08"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_gm01","q_n5u02_gm03","q_n5u02_gm04","q_n5u02_dg01","q_n5u02_dg04","q_n5u02_dg06","q_n5u02_dg07","q_n5u02_gl01"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u02_l6","unit_id":"n5_u02","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Listen and read","goal":"Hear greetings and read station signs and a shop window.","introduces":{},"explain":[{"heading":"Sounds in context","body":["Greetings are heard far more often than they are read. Listen for the number of beats and the ending of each phrase.","On signs, short words like いりぐち (entrance) and でぐち (exit) are worth learning by shape."],"examples":[{"ja":"いりぐち","reading":"iriguchi","en":"entrance"},{"ja":"でぐち","reading":"deguchi","en":"exit"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_gl01","q_n5u02_gl02","q_n5u02_gl03","q_n5u02_gl04","q_n5u02_dc01","q_n5u02_dc02","q_n5u02_dc03","q_n5u02_dc04"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_rq01","q_n5u02_rq02","q_n5u02_rq03","q_n5u02_rq04","q_n5u02_rq05","q_n5u02_gl05","q_n5u02_gl06","q_n5u02_gl07","q_n5u02_gl08"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_gl03","q_n5u02_gl05","q_n5u02_gl08","q_n5u02_rq01","q_n5u02_rq02","q_n5u02_rq04","q_n5u02_dc02"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u02_l7","unit_id":"n5_u02","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Putting words together","goal":"Use your new kana and words in short phrases, mixing in what you learned in unit 1.","introduces":{},"explain":[{"heading":"Phrases you can already read","body":["Describing words come before the noun (あたらしい くるま), の links two nouns (ともだち の いえ) and と means \"and\" (りんご と ぶどう). With more than 150 words and every hiragana, you can read many labels and signs."],"examples":[{"ja":"あたらしい くるま","reading":"atarashii kuruma","en":"a new car"},{"ja":"ともだち の いえ","reading":"tomodachi no ie","en":"a friend's house"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_tr01","q_n5u02_tr02","q_n5u02_tr03","q_n5u02_tr04","q_n5u02_tr05","q_n5u02_tr06","q_n5u02_sp01","q_n5u02_sp02","q_n5u02_sp03","q_n5u02_sp04","q_n5u02_so01","q_n5u02_so02"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_tr07","q_n5u02_tr08","q_n5u02_tr09","q_n5u02_tr10","q_n5u02_tr11","q_n5u02_tr12","q_n5u02_sp05","q_n5u02_sp06","q_n5u02_sp07","q_n5u02_sp08","q_n5u02_sp09","q_n5u02_sp10","q_n5u02_so03","q_n5u02_so04","q_n5u02_ty01","q_n5u02_ty02","q_n5u02_ty03","q_n5u02_ty04"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u02_tr02","q_n5u02_tr07","q_n5u02_tr12","q_n5u02_sp05","q_n5u02_sp08","q_n5u02_sp11","q_n5u02_sp12","q_n5u02_so02","q_n5u02_ty01","q_n5u02_ty09"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"}
